-- 130: EPFL Excellence Fellowships (Master's) (rel 10, open, 2026-12-15)
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'EPFL Excellence Fellowships (Master''s)', provider = 'EPFL (Ecole Polytechnique Federale de Lausanne)', coverage_type = 'Stipend', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'Annual: apply through EPFL''s online Master application and tick the excellence-fellowship box - the application must be paid and validated by 15 December (next: 15 December 2026 for Autumn 2027 entry); EPFL students applying for a consecutive Master''s in the same field apply to their section by 31 January.', deadline_date = '2026-12-15', deadline_type = 'fixed', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Master's"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["All"]$j$, eligible_countries = '[]', min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$To reward the most outstanding students beginning a Master's, EPFL offers a limited number of Master Excellence Fellowships worth CHF 10,000 per semester - with a maximum coverage of four semesters (two to three semesters of the Master's cycle plus the Master's project semester) - to candidates who have achieved remarkable academic results and distinguish themselves in extracurricular activities, whether sporting, artistic, civic or entrepreneurial. They are open both to students who obtained their Bachelor's at EPFL and to those who began their studies at another institution, and aim to let fellows concentrate on their Master's while building cross-disciplinary skills. External candidates additionally get a guaranteed reservation of a room in a student residence (rent remains theirs to pay), and fellows receive a certificate of excellence on completing the Master's. Students remain responsible for all living expenses including tuition fees and rent, and the fellowship cannot be combined with other substantial scholarships. Selection runs through an initial screening by the sections and a final award by the Excellence Fellowships Committee, with selected candidates notified in late March; renewal for the second year requires at least 50 credits and a weighted average of 5.0/6 - with no exceptions.$desc$, requirements = $req$Anyone applying to an EPFL Master's programme is eligible, for one Master's programme per year; candidates who already hold a Master's degree or are currently enrolled in an EPFL Master's programme are not eligible. External candidates (Bachelor's from a university abroad) apply via EPFL's online Master application form, ticking the box asking for their profile to also be considered for an excellence fellowship - only applications paid and validated by 15 December are considered for the fellowship (later applications are reviewed for admission only), and no documents beyond the admission file are required. Assessment weighs academic excellence together with achievements in research (publications, prizes), entrepreneurship and societal commitment. The 5.0/6 average with 50 credits is a renewal condition, not an entry cutoff, and no IELTS figure is published for the fellowship, so min_gpa/min_ielts are not recorded.$req$, website_url = 'https://www.epfl.ch/education/master/master-excellence-fellowships/', source_url = 'https://www.epfl.ch/education/master/master-excellence-fellowships/', application_url = 'https://www.epfl.ch/education/master/master-excellence-fellowships/how-to-apply/', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'open', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 106). The previously stored URL (epfl.ch/education/master/financial-support/excellence-fellowships) returns 404; the scheme was rewritten from EPFL's current official Master excellence fellowships page and its Application & deadlines subpage, both fetched the same day (CHF 10,000 per semester, maximum four semesters; guaranteed housing reservation for external candidates; tuition/living not waived; 15 December first-window deadline for the 2027 cycle with 31 January for EPFL-internal consecutive candidates; one programme per year; already-holding-a-Master's exclusion; renewal at 50 credits and 5.0/6). The old title conflated the fellowships with EPFL doctoral assistantships - salaried employment, not a scholarship - so the record was narrowed to the Master's scheme that the stored URL actually described, and degree_levels was corrected from PhD to Master's. award stored as CHF 20,000/year (fixed), the faithful annual equivalent of the official CHF 10,000-per-semester figure, because the award_period vocabulary has no 'semester' unit (checked against the table's distinct values); the per-semester truth is stated in funding_type. deadline_date 2026-12-15 is the next published deadline (Autumn 2027 entry) with status 'open'. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL. Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with no values read. university_scholarships row 532 synced; source 2516 repointed from the bare domain to the fetched official page.$note$, award_amount = 20000, award_currency = 'CHF', award_period = 'year', award_basis = 'fixed', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'CHF 10,000 per semester (maximum 4 semesters), i.e. CHF 20,000 per full study year, + guaranteed student-room reservation for external candidates and a certificate of excellence', tuition_coverage = 'No tuition waiver: students pay their own tuition fees, rent and living expenses (the CHF 10,000-per-semester grant, paid into a Swiss bank/postal account, is meant to help cover them).', english_requirements = 'EPFL Master admission language rules apply; the fellowship publishes no separate IELTS cutoff.', required_documents = $j$["EPFL online Master application with the excellence-fellowship box ticked (external candidates - no documents beyond the admission file)","Reference letters uploaded within one week after the 15 December deadline (exact date in the validation email)","Internal consecutive-Master candidates: CV, motivation letter, EPFL transcript and two recommendation letters sent by referees to the section"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"cycle":"Autumn 2027 entry","deadline":"2026-12-15","status":"open"},{"pattern":"Annual single window: external candidates apply via the EPFL Master online application by 15 December (paid and validated); selected candidates notified late March"}]$json$ WHERE id = 130;

-- 331: UZH Candoc Grant (rel 10)
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'UZH Candoc Grant', provider = 'University of Zurich', coverage_type = 'Salary funding', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'Annual call with a submission deadline in February (2026 call: 2 February 2026; the next call closes in February 2027 - exact date in the annual call text of the UZH Research & Grants Office).', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["PhD"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["All"]$j$, eligible_countries = '[]', min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$With the UZH Candoc Grants, the University of Zurich supports its promising early-career researchers at the doctoral level who want to work on an excellent, self-designed PhD thesis at UZH: since 2019 the Candoc and Postdoc funding lines have been called once a year, and funding goes primarily toward the grantee's own salary so as to provide protected research time, plus funds for material and travel essential to the project (up to CHF 10,000). The maximum project duration depends on the faculty - twelve months everywhere except the Faculty of Arts and Social Sciences, where up to 24 months of funding can be granted - so most candidates use a Candoc Grant as one funded segment of the doctorate rather than whole-degree funding. Salary is calculated at a fixed 80% employment level by UZH doctoral salary class (in the 2026 guidelines: CHF 50,404 for the first PhD year, CHF 52,011 for the second and CHF 53,618 for the third/fourth). Applications are assessed by the UZH Research Committee, and projects must start on the first day of a month (for the 2026 call, between 1 September 2026 and 1 September 2027).$desc$, requirements = $req$Applicants are eligible if they intend to obtain a PhD degree at the University of Zurich and, at the time of applying, are either enrolled at UZH as a PhD student or hold a binding confirmation from their future UZH PhD supervisor (first supervisor). The call guidelines add that Candoc/Postdoc grants are awarded only to candidates distinguished by above-average performance whose proposal is written independently and based on their own ideas; mobility between Master and PhD is preferable though not required, and only one Candoc or Postdoc application may be submitted per call. No nationality restriction, numeric GPA cutoff or IELTS figure is published, so min_gpa/min_ielts are not recorded.$req$, website_url = 'https://www.research.uzh.ch/en/funding/phd/uzhcandoc.html', source_url = 'https://www.research.uzh.ch/en/funding/phd/uzhcandoc.html', application_url = 'https://www.research.uzh.ch/en/funding/phd/uzhcandoc.html', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'upcoming', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 106). The previously stored URL (research.uzh.ch/en/funding/phd/candoc.html) returns 404; the scheme was rewritten from the University of Zurich's current official UZH Candoc Grant page fetched the same day (annual calls; 2019-2026 recipient lists; next call submission deadline February 2027; enrolment or binding supervisor confirmation; own salary plus limited materials; 12-month funding in most faculties, 24 months in Arts and Social Sciences) together with the official 2026 application guidelines (2 February 2026 deadline for that call; 80% employment salary classes CHF 50,404/52,011/53,618 by PhD year; materials/travel requests capped at CHF 10,000; above-average performance and independent-proposal rules; project start windows). Title corrected to the scheme's official name ('UZH Candoc Grant' - the old title padded it with 'Doctoral Grant and Fellowship'). award_amount NULL (variable): the funded salary differs by PhD year and the funded duration by faculty, so the salary classes live in funding_type. deadline_date NULL/'not_published' (the February 2027 call date is announced only to the month on the official page) with the pattern in rounds; status 'upcoming'. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL. Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with no values read. university_scholarships row 578 synced; source 2692 repointed from the bare domain to the fetched official page.$note$, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = 'year', award_basis = 'variable', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'Own salary at 80% employment (2026 salary classes: CHF 50,404 first PhD year, CHF 52,011 second, CHF 53,618 third/fourth) plus essential material/travel funds up to CHF 10,000', tuition_coverage = 'Funds the doctoral candidate''s own salary (protected research time) and limited materials rather than waiving tuition; maximum duration 12 months in most faculties and 24 months in the Faculty of Arts and Social Sciences.', english_requirements = 'No IELTS threshold is published for the grant; University of Zurich doctoral admission and the annual call guidelines apply.', required_documents = $j$["Online application submitted in the annual call to the UZH Research & Grants Office (support@research.uzh.ch)","Research proposal written independently by the applicant and based on their own ideas","Proof of enrolment as a UZH PhD student or binding confirmation from the future UZH PhD (first) supervisor"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"cycle":"2026 call","deadline":"2026-02-02","status":"closed"},{"pattern":"Called once a year with a February submission deadline (next call: February 2027); funded projects start on the first of a month - for the 2026 call between 1 September 2026 and 1 September 2027"}]$json$ WHERE id = 331;

-- 341: University of Geneva Excellence Master Fellowships (rel 10)
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'University of Geneva Excellence Master Fellowships', provider = 'University of Geneva, Faculty of Science', coverage_type = 'Living-expenses grant', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'Annual: applications are made online from the beginning of January each year; the most recent published deadline was 28 February 2026 (for Masters starting 14 September 2026) - each cycle''s date is published on the Faculty of Science page.', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Master's"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["Astronomy","Biology","Chemistry and Biochemistry","Computer Science","Mathematics","Physics","Pharmaceutical Sciences","Earth Sciences"]$j$, eligible_countries = '[]', min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$The Faculty of Science of the University of Geneva - whose research spans astronomy, biology, chemistry and biochemistry, computer science, mathematics, physics, pharmaceutical sciences and earth sciences, and which hosts two Swiss National Centres of Competence in Research (SwissMAP and Planets) - runs, with the support of external partners, an Excellence Fellowship programme for outstanding and highly motivated students who wish to pursue a Master of Science in one of the Faculty's disciplines; the Faculty's Masters are taught entirely in English or in English and French. The fellowship is a grant of CHF 10,000 to CHF 15,000 per year with no teaching duties: it is awarded for one year and extended for the regular duration of the chosen Master's programme (three or four semesters) provided the fellow is academically successful at the end of the first semester. The programme is addressed to brilliant bachelor students who are among the best in their year, regardless of their home university - but students who have already started a Master programme at the Faculty of Science can no longer apply.$desc$, requirements = $req$Applicants must have passed - or be completing with excellent results - a bachelor degree and be among the best in their year, meet the admission criteria of their chosen Master of Science at the Faculty of Science, and have completed the University of Geneva enrolment procedure (current UNIGE students submit a scan of their UNIGE card; others submit the registration-confirmation e-mail as proof of having begun enrolment). Selection is based on excellence, assessed from a single-PDF application (CV, bachelor transcript with all grades, motivation letter, two professors' reference letters; GRE/TOEFL or other language-test results may be added as pertinent information). Students who have already started a Master at the Faculty are ineligible, and incomplete applications are not considered. No numeric GPA or IELTS cutoff is published, so min_gpa/min_ielts are not recorded.$req$, website_url = 'https://www.unige.ch/sciences/en/enseignements/formations/masters/excellencemasterfellowships/', source_url = 'https://www.unige.ch/sciences/en/enseignements/formations/masters/excellencemasterfellowships/', application_url = 'https://www.unige.ch/sciences/en/enseignements/formations/masters/excellencemasterfellowships/', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'upcoming', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 106). The previously stored URL (unige.ch/sciences/en/enseignements/formations/master/excellence-master-fellowships) returns 'Page introuvable'; the scheme was rewritten from the UNIGE Faculty of Science's current official Excellence Master Fellowships page fetched the same day (CHF 10,000-15,000 per year, no teaching duties; one year extended for the regular three-to-four-semester duration if successful after the first semester; Faculty-of-Science disciplines; best-in-year bachelor profile; enrolment-procedure prerequisite; already-started exclusion; single-PDF application from the beginning of January; latest published deadline 28 February 2026 for a 14 September 2026 start). award_amount NULL with basis 'range' (a CHF 10,000-15,000 yearly band). deadline_date NULL/'not_published': only the passed cycle's date is currently published on the official page, so no next date was extrapolated - the annual January-opening/late-February-deadline pattern is recorded in rounds; status 'upcoming'. eligible_majors now lists the eight Faculty disciplines (the record previously implied university-wide scope). min_gpa/min_ielts NULL. Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with no values read. university_scholarships row 659 synced; source 2667 repointed from the bare domain to the fetched official page.$note$, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = 'year', award_basis = 'range', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'Grant of CHF 10,000 to CHF 15,000 per year (no teaching duties); awarded for one year and extended for the regular duration of the Master (3-4 semesters) if academically successful after the first semester', tuition_coverage = 'A yearly living-expenses grant; the fellowship includes no tuition-fee waiver.', english_requirements = 'The Faculty''s Masters are taught entirely in English or in English and French depending on the programme; the fellowship sets no IELTS cutoff (TOEFL/GRE results may be included in the application as supporting evidence).', required_documents = $j$["Single-PDF online application: scan of national identity card or passport","Curriculum vitae (2 pages maximum) and transcript of the bachelor education with all grades","Motivation letter on scientific interests and motivation for the Geneva Master of Science","Reference letters from two professors","Proof of the UNIGE enrolment procedure (UNIGE card scan or the registration-confirmation e-mail)"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"pattern":"Annual: online applications open at the beginning of January; the most recent published deadline was 28 February 2026 for Masters starting 14 September 2026"}]$json$ WHERE id = 341;

-- 409: UNIL Master's Scholarship (rel 10, open, 2026-11-01)
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'UNIL Master''s Scholarship (University of Lausanne)', provider = 'University of Lausanne (UNIL)', coverage_type = 'Stipend + Registration-fee Exemption', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = '1 November each year (online registration and PDF file, recommendation letters, and certified copies by post where required); the 2027/2028 round is open until 1 November 2026, with decisions notified in early April 2027.', deadline_date = '2026-11-01', deadline_type = 'fixed', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Master's"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["All UNIL Master programmes except: Medicine; Sciences and Practices of Education; Law (except International and Comparative Law, Legal Theory, International Tax Law and Policy); Physical Education and Sport Didactics; Health Sciences; Sustainable Management & Technology; Human Taphonomy; all MAS programmes"]$j$, eligible_countries = '[]', min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$The Unil Master's Scholarship is the University of Lausanne's excellence grant for a limited number of outstanding graduates of foreign universities entering an eligible UNIL Master's programme: it pays CHF 1,600 per month for the minimum statutory period of the chosen programme, and recipients are exempt from the standard course registration fees (only the CHF 80 semester fees remain payable). UNIL is explicit that this is not full funding - the authorities reckon roughly CHF 2,000 per month is needed to live in Lausanne, so complementary resources are strongly recommended - although all scholarship holders are guaranteed accommodation with the Lausanne Student Housing Foundation (FMEL) at reasonable rent. Conveniently, the scholarship application also serves as the application to the chosen Master's degree, so there is no separate admission application; complete files are screened by the Social Affairs and Student Mobility Service (SASME) and the Admissions Office, considered by the faculties, and the Selection Board decides in March, with applicants notified in early April (decisions may not be appealed). Withdrawing from the Master programme suspends the scholarship.$desc$, requirements = $req$Applicants must hold - or complete before starting the Master - a foreign university degree recognised as equivalent to a Swiss university bachelor (180 ECTS), with outstanding ('very high level') academic results; degrees must come from a foreign university only. They must not be currently enrolled at UNIL (students who have already begun a Master at UNIL or are in a preparatory year cannot apply), must demonstrate a minimum CEFR C1 level in the language of instruction of the chosen programme (French or English), and must pay the non-refundable administrative fee of CHF 200. There is no age limit. Several programmes are excluded (Medicine; Sciences and Practices of Education; Law except three specialisms; Physical Education and Sport Didactics; Health Sciences; Sustainable Management & Technology; Human Taphonomy; all MAS programmes), and additional conditions apply for Finance, Psychology, Arts and Nursing. No grade list by country and no IELTS figure is published - the C1 standard is evidenced by the programme's official language certificate - so min_gpa/min_ielts are not recorded.$req$, website_url = 'https://www.unil.ch/unil/en/home/menuinst/etudier/mobilite-et-echange/etudiantes-et-etudiants-internationaux/etudiantes-internationaux-reguliers/bourse-de-master.html', source_url = 'https://www.unil.ch/unil/en/home/menuinst/etudier/mobilite-et-echange/etudiantes-et-etudiants-internationaux/etudiantes-internationaux-reguliers/bourse-de-master.html', application_url = 'https://www.unil.ch/unil/en/home/menuinst/etudier/mobilite-et-echange/etudiantes-et-etudiants-internationaux/etudiantes-internationaux-reguliers/bourse-de-master.html', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'open', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 106). The previously stored URL (unil.ch/international/.../bourses-master-de-lunil.html) returns 404; the scheme was rewritten from the University of Lausanne's current official 'Unil Master's Scholarship' page fetched the same day, including its eligibility conditions, excluded programmes, single-PDF plus two-letter procedure, certified-copies rule for diplomas from states that have not ratified the Lisbon Convention, the November-to-April selection calendar, the open 2027/2028 round ('The deadline is 1 November 2026'), the not-full-funding warning (~CHF 2,000/month needed) and the FMEL housing guarantee. Title updated to the scheme's current official name. award CHF 1,600/month with basis 'fixed' (the single published monthly figure, for the programme's minimum statutory duration). deadline_date 2026-11-01 is the currently open round's published deadline with status 'open'. The approximately-ten-grants quota quoted by scholarship portals was not stated on the parts of the official page read, so no quota is recorded. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL (the language standard is CEFR C1 in the programme's language). Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with no values read. university_scholarships row 622 synced; source 2668 repointed from the bare domain to the fetched official page.$note$, award_amount = 1600, award_currency = 'CHF', award_period = 'month', award_basis = 'fixed', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'CHF 1,600/month for the minimum statutory duration of the Master programme + exemption from standard course registration fees; not full funding (UNIL estimates about CHF 2,000/month is needed in Lausanne; FMEL student housing is guaranteed)', tuition_coverage = 'Recipients are exempt from the standard course registration fees; only the semester fees of CHF 80 remain payable.', english_requirements = 'Minimum CEFR C1 in the language of instruction of the chosen programme (French for French-taught, English for English-taught programmes), evidenced by the official language certificate where required.', required_documents = $j$["Online registration with a single-PDF application file: CV with photo, covering letter (1-2 pages), university diplomas and all official transcripts (authenticated translation unless in French, German, English or Italian), description of the final bachelor year/semester if the degree is pending, official C1 language certificate where required, secondary school leaving diploma, passport copy","Proof of payment of the CHF 200 administrative fee (non-refundable)","Two letters of recommendation sent by their authors from a professional e-mail address to mastergrants@unil.ch by 1 November (only after online registration)","Certified true copies of diplomas/transcripts sealed by the issuing university and sent by post to SASME, if the diploma state has not ratified the Lisbon Convention"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"cycle":"2027/2028 entry (September 2027)","deadline":"2026-11-01","status":"open"},{"pattern":"Annual: 1 November application deadline (online file, letters and certified copies); faculties consider eligibility January-February; Selection Board decides in March; applicants notified in early April; decisions may not be appealed"}]$json$ WHERE id = 409;

-- 407: retired (Basel funding-options directory under a generic invented name)
UPDATE scholarships SET is_active = false, application_status = 'closed', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = NULL, tuition_coverage = NULL, english_requirements = NULL, required_documents = NULL, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = NULL, notes = $note$Retired on 2026-10-27 after official-source review: no University of Basel scheme named 'University of Basel PhD Fellowships' exists. The previously stored URL (unibas.ch/en/Research/Financing-Doctorate.html) returns 404, and the university's current official Doctoral Candidates individual-funding page (fetched 2026-10-27) is an overview directory of financing routes rather than a single award: doctorates are financed primarily through supervisor-led SNSF projects and research-associate positions ('you cannot solve the funding question by yourself - please contact your professor'), supplemented by distinct narrow instruments such as the Research Fund for outstanding junior researchers (dissertation-completion salary for enrolled PhD students in named faculties, applications up to CHF 80,000), doctoral-programme start-up grants, the Burckhardt-Buergin Foundation's short-stay travel grants (cap CHF 5,000), a private-foundations directory and the 'get on track' line for doctoral parents. A generic title draped over a directory of financing options is not a single scholarship, and rewriting the row into one of these unrelated internal instruments would violate the cleanup's identity rule, so the record is retired. Kept for audit only; not a discoverable scholarship. university_scholarships row 619 withdrawn; source 2664 repointed to the fetched official Doctoral Candidates funding overview.$note$, last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 407;

-- 408: retired (Bern funding-schemes overview under a generic invented name)
UPDATE scholarships SET is_active = false, application_status = 'closed', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = NULL, tuition_coverage = NULL, english_requirements = NULL, required_documents = NULL, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = NULL, notes = $note$Retired on 2026-10-27 after official-source review: no University of Bern scheme named 'University of Bern Doctoral Grants' exists as a single scholarship. The previously stored URL (unibe.ch/research/funding/doctoral_students) is dead, and the university's current official UniBE Funding Schemes page (fetched 2026-10-27) lists a portfolio of small internal instruments - the postdoc-level Initiator Grant (up to CHF 30,000), the Promotion Fund (up to CHF 5,000 for networking), UniBE Doc.Mobility (6-12 month research stays abroad for doctoral students already enrolled at Bern for at least 12 months and not SNSF-funded), Short Travel Grants (up to CHF 8,000 for 2-8 week stays), innovation and infrastructure funds - while Bern's own doctorate guidance states that a doctorate is funded in most cases through assistant/doctoral qualification positions or SNSF funding. An overview of positions, external funder routes and top-up grants is a directory, not a scholarship a prospective applicant can apply for, so the record is retired (none of the listed micro-instruments matches the stored record's identity). Kept for audit only; not a discoverable scholarship. university_scholarships row 126 withdrawn; source 2665 repointed to the fetched official UniBE funding-schemes overview. A future additions batch could consider UniBE Doc.Mobility as its own record only if cataloguing enrolled-student mobility grants is ever in scope.$note$, last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 408;

-- sources: repoint exclusive bare-domain sources to the fetched official pages
UPDATE sources SET url = CASE id WHEN 2516 THEN 'https://www.epfl.ch/education/master/master-excellence-fellowships/' WHEN 2692 THEN 'https://www.research.uzh.ch/en/funding/phd/uzhcandoc.html' WHEN 2667 THEN 'https://www.unige.ch/sciences/en/enseignements/formations/masters/excellencemasterfellowships/' WHEN 2664 THEN 'https://www.unibas.ch/en/Research/Individual-Funding/Doctoral-Candidates.html' WHEN 2665 THEN 'https://www.unibe.ch/research/funding_and_prizes/unibe_funding_schemes/index_eng.html' WHEN 2668 THEN 'https://www.unil.ch/unil/en/home/menuinst/etudier/mobilite-et-echange/etudiantes-et-etudiants-internationaux/etudiantes-internationaux-reguliers/bourse-de-master.html' ELSE url END, title = CASE id WHEN 2516 THEN 'Master Excellence Fellowships - EPFL Official Scheme Page' WHEN 2692 THEN 'UZH Candoc Grant - University of Zurich Research & Grants Office' WHEN 2667 THEN 'Excellence Master Fellowships - UNIGE Faculty of Science' WHEN 2664 THEN 'Doctoral Candidates (Individual Funding overview) - University of Basel' WHEN 2665 THEN 'UniBE Funding Schemes (overview) - University of Bern' WHEN 2668 THEN 'Unil Master''s Scholarship - University of Lausanne' ELSE title END, domain = CASE id WHEN 2516 THEN 'epfl.ch' WHEN 2692 THEN 'research.uzh.ch' WHEN 2667 THEN 'unige.ch' WHEN 2664 THEN 'unibas.ch' WHEN 2665 THEN 'unibe.ch' WHEN 2668 THEN 'unil.ch' ELSE domain END, accessed_at = now(), is_verified = true WHERE id IN (2516,2692,2667,2664,2665,2668);

-- university_scholarships: 4 synced (532, 578, 659, 622) + 2 withdrawn (619, 126)
UPDATE university_scholarships SET scholarship_name = CASE id WHEN 532 THEN 'EPFL Excellence Fellowships (Master''s)' WHEN 578 THEN 'UZH Candoc Grant' WHEN 659 THEN 'University of Geneva Excellence Master Fellowships' WHEN 619 THEN 'University of Basel PhD Fellowships (retired: generic title over a funding-options overview)' WHEN 126 THEN 'University of Bern Doctoral Grants (retired: generic title over a funding-schemes overview)' WHEN 622 THEN 'UNIL Master''s Scholarship (University of Lausanne)' ELSE scholarship_name END, availability_status = CASE WHEN id IN (619,126) THEN 'No' ELSE availability_status END, funding_type = CASE id WHEN 532 THEN 'Excellence fellowship: CHF 10,000 per semester (max 4 semesters)' WHEN 578 THEN 'Own doctoral salary (80% employment) + materials up to CHF 10,000' WHEN 659 THEN 'Grant of CHF 10,000-15,000/year, no teaching duties' WHEN 619 THEN 'Retired directory/generic entry (2026-10-27)' WHEN 126 THEN 'Retired directory/generic entry (2026-10-27)' WHEN 622 THEN 'CHF 1,600/month grant + registration-fee exemption' ELSE funding_type END, max_scholarship = CASE id WHEN 532 THEN 'CHF 10,000 per semester for up to 4 semesters + guaranteed student-room reservation (external candidates); tuition not waived' WHEN 578 THEN '2026 salary classes at 80% employment: CHF 50,404 / 52,011 / 53,618 per year by PhD year, for 12 months (24 in Arts & Social Sciences)' WHEN 659 THEN 'CHF 10,000-15,000 per year, extended for the regular Master duration (3-4 semesters)' WHEN 619 THEN 'No single award of this name: doctorate financing runs through supervisor-led SNSF projects and positions' WHEN 126 THEN 'No single award of this name: doctorates are funded via qualification positions and SNSF funding' WHEN 622 THEN 'CHF 1,600/month for the minimum statutory duration + course registration fee exemption (CHF 80/semester remains payable)' ELSE max_scholarship END, covers_tuition = CASE id WHEN 532 THEN false WHEN 578 THEN false WHEN 659 THEN false WHEN 622 THEN true ELSE covers_tuition END, covers_living_expenses = CASE id WHEN 532 THEN true WHEN 578 THEN true WHEN 659 THEN true WHEN 622 THEN true ELSE covers_living_expenses END, official_url = CASE id WHEN 532 THEN 'https://www.epfl.ch/education/master/master-excellence-fellowships/' WHEN 578 THEN 'https://www.research.uzh.ch/en/funding/phd/uzhcandoc.html' WHEN 659 THEN 'https://www.unige.ch/sciences/en/enseignements/formations/masters/excellencemasterfellowships/' WHEN 622 THEN 'https://www.unil.ch/unil/en/home/menuinst/etudier/mobilite-et-echange/etudiantes-et-etudiants-internationaux/etudiantes-internationaux-reguliers/bourse-de-master.html' ELSE official_url END, source_url = CASE id WHEN 532 THEN 'https://www.epfl.ch/education/master/master-excellence-fellowships/' WHEN 578 THEN 'https://www.research.uzh.ch/en/funding/phd/uzhcandoc.html' WHEN 659 THEN 'https://www.unige.ch/sciences/en/enseignements/formations/masters/excellencemasterfellowships/' WHEN 622 THEN 'https://www.unil.ch/unil/en/home/menuinst/etudier/mobilite-et-echange/etudiantes-et-etudiants-internationaux/etudiantes-internationaux-reguliers/bourse-de-master.html' ELSE source_url END, verification_status = CASE WHEN id IN (619,126) THEN 'withdrawn' ELSE 'verified' END, last_verified_at = now() WHERE id IN (532,578,659,619,126,622);
